# Everything ships with LF endings, whatever the cloning machine's core.autocrlf says.
#
# scripts/run.sh is the reason this file exists. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would hand Windows installers a run.sh full of CRLF,
# and bash treats the trailing \r as part of the last token on every line, so the
# hook dies with an unreadable error. Python and JSON are fine either way, but
# normalising the whole tree keeps diffs clean too.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
